gab-001 fix: SIMD `gab_smooth` mul_add → explicit Mul+Add (libjxl-parity)
============================================================================

## What was measured

5 production cells encoded twice from the same workspace at the same git
parent (jj `oyozsvzm a11fd0e2`) with the ONLY difference being the
SIMD `gab_smooth_avx2` / `gab_smooth_neon` inner loop:

- PRE-fix: `wc_v.mul_add(center, w1_v.mul_add(cardinals, w2_v * diagonals))`
  (2 FMAs + 1 mul → 3 chained roundings into a fused single-rounding tree)
- POST-fix: `wc_v * center + w1_v * cardinals + w2_v * diagonals`
  (3 muls + 2 adds → 5 explicit roundings, matches libjxl
  `convolve_symmetric5.cc:66-69` `WeightedSum` `Mul` + `Add` pattern)

Bench harness: `jxl-encoder/examples/gab_001_bench.rs`, registered under
`required-features = ["__expert"]`, run via `cargo run --release
--features __expert --example gab_001_bench`.

Build command for both runs:
  cargo run --release --features __expert --example gab_001_bench

PRE-fix run: temporarily reverted gab.rs to the mul_add shape, ran the
bench, recorded bytes + SHA8.
POST-fix run: restored gab.rs to the explicit-Mul+Add shape, ran the
bench, recorded bytes + SHA8.

## Cells

1. cid22_1418519 e7 d=1   (512x512 CID22 photo, photo-class)
2. gb82_codec_wiki e7 d=2 (2560x1664 wiki-page screenshot, mixed-content)
3. gb82_terminal e8 d=4   (1646x1078 terminal screenshot, text-heavy)
4. gb82_imac_dark e6 d=0.5 (2940x1840 dark-themed screenshot, high-contrast)
5. synthetic_gradient e7 d=1 (64x64 RGB gradient, smooth)

## Headline result

5/5 cells: BYTES IDENTICAL (delta_bytes = 0 on every cell, delta_pct = 0.000)
3/5 cells: SHA IDENTICAL (terminal, imac_dark, gradient)
2/5 cells: SHA DIVERGED but same byte count (cid22_1418519, codec_wiki)

The byte counts being identical is structural: gab's f32 output is fed
into the quantizer which integer-rounds; the ULP-scale shift from
mul_add fusion vs explicit Mul+Add is absorbed by quantization rounding
on every cell tested. The 2 SHA-diverged cells indicate that the
QUANTIZED-coefficient bitstream layout shifted slightly (some quant
codes flipped at the ±0.5 boundary) but the entropy coder produced the
same total byte count.

This is the SAME pattern documented in W44-RECON-DEEP/A11 (`91fb35a8`)
where the XYB→linear FMA fix was BYTE-IDENTICAL on 8/8 cells. Buttloop
+ quantizer + entropy coder are robust to ULP-scale numeric divergence
on production-relevant inputs; the right reason to make the fix is
LIBJXL PARITY (decoder-side gaborish, byte-exact reconstruction
consistency with the cjxl reference), not encoder bytes/quality
improvement.

## Acceptance gates (all PASS)

(a) Build PASS on every feature combo touched.
(b) `cargo test -p jxl-encoder-simd` 181/181 PASS. `gab` tests 7/7 PASS
    INCLUDING the previously-`#[ignore]`d `gab_scalar_vs_dispatch_sizes_strict`.
(c) `cargo test -p jxl-encoder --lib --features "__expert __internals"`
    1505/1505 PASS.
(d) drift 7/7 PASS, byte-lock 4/4 BYTE-IDENTICAL (NO regen needed),
    hash-locks 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL (NO regen needed).
(e) This bench TSV.
(f) `docs/SIMD_PARITY_KNOWN_DIVERGENCES.md` gab-001 flipped to RESOLVED.
(g) `docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md` Section G new row for gab-001.
(h) Single commit pushed via jj git push to origin/main.
(i) Sibling workspace cleaned up per CLAUDE.md.

## DO NOT

- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the divergence (per W44-66 user
  correction). The divergence is specifically the `mul_add` FUSION
  tree-shape vs the explicit Mul+Add tree-shape — both fully precise.
  libjxl chose Mul+Add; we now match.
- DO NOT respawn this chunk thinking the byte-identical result is
  evidence the fix is unnecessary. The fix's value is LIBJXL PARITY of
  the gaborish convolution shape, which closes:
    1. gab-001 SIMD-vs-scalar divergence (was tolerated via #[ignore])
    2. SIMD-vs-libjxl convolution shape divergence
    3. The last `#[ignore]`d SIMD-parity test in jxl-encoder-simd
- DO NOT revert the AVX2 `mul_add` chain back. It is faster on FMA
  hardware but produces output that does NOT match libjxl's
  reference convolution — exactly the kind of divergence the
  SIMD-parity audit (eedc1877 + fb871c83) was built to surface.
- DO NOT add a runtime feature flag to switch back to mul_add on
  encode-only paths. The scalar path was already libjxl-shape; SIMD
  must match libjxl + scalar = ONE behaviour, not two.
